commenti.body:
When I was a teenager, I hated 2001: A Space Odyssey. I had no idea why it was highly acclaimed. Nothing happens, it's very slow and none of the characters were interesting. I knew there had to be something about it that people liked, so I read reviews and watched video essays on it. It soon clicked, there was a point where I went "ohh that's what it's about". 2001 is now one of my all time favourite movies.

&#x200B;

With challenging films, you have to approach them at a different angle. You have to swim out and meet the boat halfway. Reading reviews/analyses/essays on films you don't understand can help you develop an appreciation. Understaning what the movie is about is the first step toward enjoying it.

&#x200B;

Why is Tár entertaining? For one, that's extremely subjective. I personally find Tár to be very  entertaining, I could watch that film back-to-back even before untangling all its metaphors. It's fine if you find a movie boring, it happens. The type of story Tár is trying to tell calls for subtlety. It wouldn't be the same film if the dramatic conflict were more obvious. The type of storytelling in Tár simply resonates with enough people to give it acclaim.
